Report read errors in rev.
fgets() returns NULL on a read error just as at end of file, and rev
never checked the stream's error flag, so it stopped quietly with
status 0. Close the file with fclose_if_not_stdin(), which reports the
error flag, print the file name with the error, and exit with status 1.
This also stops rev from closing standard input, so "rev - -" no longer
reads from a closed stream.

---
 util-linux/rev.c |    5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/util-linux/rev.c
+++ b/util-linux/rev.c
@@ -118,7 +118,10 @@
 			fputs_stdout(buf);
 			pos = 0;
 		}
-		fclose(fp);
+		if (fclose_if_not_stdin(fp)) {
+			bb_simple_perror_msg(argv[-1]);
+			retval = EXIT_FAILURE;
+		}
 	} while (*argv);
 
 	if (ENABLE_FEATURE_CLEAN_UP)
